# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
build/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
yarn-debug.log*

# Expo
.expo/
.expo-shared/

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Claude Code. agents/ and skills/ ARE tracked: they carry standing
# instructions that enter every session, and until now no reviewing
# role - owner, red team, git log, any diff - could see them.
# settings.local.json stays out: per-machine trust, absolute paths,
# a dev credential. MEASURED: this must be `.claude/*`, never
# `.claude/` - a negation under an ignored DIRECTORY is inert,
# because git never descends into it to read the negation.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
# ...but the gate's own audit log is runtime data, not config. These two
# patterns come AFTER the negation on purpose: the last match wins.
.claude/hooks/*.log
.claude/hooks/*.log.1

# A third-party skill install landed under .claude/skills/ and none of it
# was ignored, while `git add *` is pre-approved in settings.local.json -
# so one sweeping stage would have committed somebody else's tree.
# The DEFAULT here is IGNORE and the AUTHORED skills are named back in,
# so the next install is excluded without anybody remembering and a new
# authored skill has to be admitted on purpose. Naming the intruders
# instead would fail open.
# MEASURED 2026-08-17 in a throwaway repository outside this tree, 14
# probes over three patterns. Today's: 5 wrong, and `git add -A` staged
# 8 third-party paths. The DIRECTORY form `.claude/skills/` (no star):
# all nine negations INERT - it re-ignores the authored skills too, and
# the damage is silent because a rule cannot untrack a tracked file, so
# `git status` looks right and only the NEXT file added inside a skill
# goes missing. This pattern: 0 and 0. The star is load-bearing for the
# same measured reason it is one level up.
# The negation count MUST EQUAL the tracked directory count -
# `git ls-files .claude/skills | cut -d/ -f3 | sort -u` returned 9 on
# 2026-08-17, and a list short by one drops a skill silently.
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/async-python-engineering/
!.claude/skills/buddhist-method/
!.claude/skills/crash-safety/
!.claude/skills/debug-mantra/
!.claude/skills/defensive-coding/
!.claude/skills/delivery-workflow/
!.claude/skills/long-running-jobs/
!.claude/skills/scrutinize/
!.claude/skills/verification-discipline/

# The same installer's other two artefacts. skills-lock.json is what ties
# them together: every entry in it records "source": "mattpocock/skills",
# and none of the nine authored skills appears in it at all.
.agents/
skills-lock.json
